Z||000000||Jncomutt||12-05-2001||03:52 PM||||Hey, just got my new exhaust installed.  I switched my coupe tail over to the GT style to allow for the duel exhaust.  ANyone know how to record the sound?/?  You guys have GOT to hear it!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||tesmith66||12-05-2001||04:21 PM||||Run a long microphone cable out to the car (get it as close to the computer as possible) and use windows sound recorder.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||12-13-2001||11:09 PM||||Here are the pics....<BR>Notice the custom cross over design.  I'm not running a muffler on my 4 cyl. and hoped this would evenly distribute the gasses so all doesn't pour outta one side, while the other just barely breaths.  Needless to say it worked.  Since its been cold, I've noticed the exhaust coming out evenly. <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Frombelow.JPG">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MiddleUnder.JPG">    <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/UnderLeft.JPG">  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/UnderRight.JPG">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FromTop.JPG">    Lookin down in the eng. compartment.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 12-13-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 12-13-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
